[117.742218, "i", "cat > docs/BILL-212.md <<'EOF'\n# BILL-212 release summary\n\nFixed proration to follow finance's rev. 4 rules.\n\n- Calendar arithmetic previously forced anchor days to the 28th and advanced\n  from prior renewals. Renewals now clamp to the target month's last day and\n  always derive from the original anchor, restoring month-end and leap-day dates.\n- Credits and same-interval charges now use actual cycle lengths instead of\n  fixed 30/365-day denominators. Credits use the old price at cycle start;\n  new charges use the price on the change date.\n- Monthly/annual switches now charge the full new price, re-anchor on the\n  change date, and set the next renewal using the new interval.\n- Half-even rounding now uses exact integer arithmetic, avoiding intermediate\n  Decimal rounding. Cycle lookup is constant-time rather than walking renewals.\n\nPublic function signatures are unchanged. Added regression tests for calendar\nboundaries, exact rounding, and invoice previews for all ten finance examples.\n\nValidation: all 24 tests"]
[117.742507, "o", "cat > docs/BILL-212.md <<'EOF'"]
[117.742526, "i", " pass with `python -m unittest discover -s tests`.\nActual `python -m billing preview` subprocesses also matched all ten examples.\nBulk repricing: 4,000 changes in 0.0375s against the existing 0.2s budget.\nNo existing tests, fixtures, known-failure entries, or budgets were changed.\nEOF\ncd /app && python -m unittest discover -s tests\n"]
[117.742536, "o", "\r\n"]
[117.742693, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[117.744256, "o", "> # BILL-212 release summary\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Fixed proration to follow finance's rev. 4 rules.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Calendar arithmetic previously forced anchor days to the 28th and advanced\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   from prior renewals. Renewals now clamp to the target month's last day and\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   always derive from the original anchor, restoring month-end and leap-day dates.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Credits and same-interval charges now use actual cycle lengths instead of\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   fixed 30/365-day denominators. Credits use the old price at cycle start;\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   new charges use the price on the change date.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Monthly/annual switches now charge the full new price, re-anchor on the\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   change date, and set the next renewal using the new interval.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Half-even rounding now uses exact integer arithmetic, avoiding intermediate\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   Decimal rounding. Cycle lookup"]
[117.744334, "o", " is constant-time rather than walking renewals.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Public function signatures are unchanged. Added regression tests for calendar\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> boundaries, exact rounding, and invoice previews for all ten finance examples.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Validation: all 24 tests pass with `python -m unittest discover -s tests`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Actual `python -m billing preview` subprocesses also matched all ten examples.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Bulk repricing: 4,000 changes in 0.0375s against the existing 0.2s budget.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> No existing tests, fixtures, known-failure entries, or budgets were changed.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
